; Form 0 produces a diagnostic and no value; forms 1..8 still evaluate.
; Both halves matter. The diagnostic is the point of the case — a runtime
; domain failure is reported, not swallowed — and the eight surviving
; values are what proves the report costs one result rather than the run.
; Had the old `std.math.clamp` assert survived, no index would be here at
; all.
;
; The path is empty because the eval pass anchors at the form's head span
; rather than at a schema slot: there is no declared path to name, the
; arguments type-check, and it is the computed values that are out of
; domain.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code expr_type_mismatch :path []))
(values
  (value :index 1 :result 2.5)
  (value :index 2 :result 15)
  (value :index 3 :result -5)
  (value :index 4 :result 1)
  (value :index 5 :result 5)
  (value :index 6 :result 1)
  (value :index 7 :result 3)
  (value :index 8 :result 5))
